+## Due dates and overdue todos
+
+`POST /todos` accepts an optional `due_date`: a calendar date string `YYYY-MM-DD` (for example `"2026-11-30"`)
+or `null`, the default. Anything else (impossible dates such as `2027-02-29`, datetimes, numbers, padded strings)
+is rejected with 422 and nothing is stored. Past dates are accepted. A due date cannot be changed after creation.
+
+Every todo the API returns carries `due_date` (`null` when unset) and a boolean `overdue`, computed when the
+response is built and never stored:
+
+```json
+{"id": 1, "title": "Pay rent", "done": false, "created_at": "2026-10-10T08:10:54.068302+00:00", "due_date": "2026-11-30", "overdue": false}
+```
+
+A todo is overdue when it is open (`done` is false) and its `due_date` is strictly before the current UTC
+calendar date. A todo due today (UTC) is not overdue, a completed todo never is, and neither is one without a
+due date. `GET /todos/overdue` returns exactly the overdue todos in ascending id order, or `[]` when there are none.
+
 ## Use it as the factory's target
 
