From 93ced45f6f75c244414e70df150301f72e81f147 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 12:33:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] AC-4: pin the UTC half of the overdue rule (review F-2)

pytest pins app.storage's clock at 1999-12-31T23:30Z, when a UTC+10 host already reads
2000-01-01, and asserts today_utc() is 1999-12-31. local-all now starts the server with a
TZ whose calendar date differs from UTC at run time, so boundary, listing and overdue-list
fail on a server that judges by its local date.
---
 tests/e2e_overdue.py  | 13 ++++++++-----
 tests/test_overdue.py | 19 ++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 26 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/e2e_overdue.py b/tests/e2e_overdue.py
index 8301e2b..193b1df 100644
--- a/tests/e2e_overdue.py
+++ b/tests/e2e_overdue.py
@@ -9,9 +9,9 @@
 <check> is a key of CHECKS below, or `all` to run every check in that order. Each check creates its own todos and
 asserts only on those ids plus single-response invariants, so it passes on an instance already holding todos.
